lpdesk\nabout\nULink\nabout\nSTUDENTS:\nCardSmart\nClass schedule\nHousing portal\nCardinal Careers\nCampus Store\nSee all\nFACULTY & STAFF:\nWorkday\nHuman Resources\nDirectory\nCampus Solutions\nUofL Folio\nSee all\nGraduate School\nApply Now\nRequest Info\nFaculty & Staff Resources\nSite Search\nGraduate School\nAll of UofL\nSearch\nSearch\nClose Search Tray\nAdmissions\nHow to Apply\nWhy UofL?\nPrepare for Graduate School\nConnect with UofL\nInternational Applicants\nAdmitted Students\nAdmission FAQs\nAcademics & Research\nPrograms & Degrees\nResearch\nGraduate Catalog\nGraduate Faculty\nDGS List\nPolicies and Procedures\nMilestones & Degree Completion\nUofL Facts & Figures\nFrequently Asked Questions\nFunding, Tuition & Aid\nTuition & Cost of Attendance\nFunding Opportunities\nFunding Policies\nFunding Questions\nFunded Student Checklist\nGraduate Student Life\nInclusive Excellence\nGraduate Student Groups\nLife in Louisville\nResilience and Wellbeing\nAwards and Recognition\nGraduate Student Resources\nProfessional Development\nWhat's Your PLAN?\nPrograms & Events\nGraduate Teaching Assistants\nMentorCenter\nCareer Development\nProfessional Development Resources\nAbout Us\nMessage from the Dean\nUnits and Offices\nGraduate School Staff\nContact Us\nGraduate News\nGraduate Newsletters\nBreadcrumb\nHome\n.....\nHome\nAdmissions Main\nHow to Apply\nApplication Fee Waiver Information\nApplication Fee Waiver Information\nReview our information to find out if you qualify for a fee waiver for your graduate application.\nApply Now\nRequest Information\nabout\nAlready Applied? Upload Your Fee Waiver Documentation Today!\nSidebar\nIn this section\nHow to Apply\nAdmissions Policies\nApplication Fee Waiver Information\nApplication Requirements\nUnderstanding Your Application Status Portal\nThe Graduate School is limited by the types of application fee waivers it can provide each year.\nCurrently only military-connected students and those receiving public assistance (from the U.S. government) may be exempt from the application fee and request an application fee waiver with appropriate documentation.\nGeneral Fee Waiver Opportunities\nVeterans, and/or those serving Active-Duty, in the National Guard, in the Reserves, in the U.S. Army, the U.S. Navy, the U.S. Air Force, the U.S. Marine Corps or the U.S. Coast Guard.\nBe sure to visit our Center for Military-Connected Students to learn how the University supports its military-connected students.\nParticipation in one of the following:\nMedicaid\nS.N.A.P. (Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program, formerly known as EBT and Food Stamps Program)\nSupplemental Security Insurance (SSI)\nRequired Documentation for General Fee Waivers\nDocumentation is required for military fee waiver requests and for any U.S. government benefit program fee waiver requests. Documentation can be uploaded to your application or sent to our service account gradadm@louisville.edu.\nApplication fee waiver documentation must contain the applicant\u2019s name, and may include, but is not limited to:\nIDs, DD 214, or military orders\nMost recent correspondence\nVerification document or letter\nProgram-Based Fee Waiver Opportunities\nProgram-based fee waivers are occasionally granted by academic departments.\u202f\u202fPlease contact your departmental admissions coordinator for information regarding fee waiver opportunities.\nBegin your graduate education journey with us!\nApply Now\nRequest Information\nTop\nContact Us\nPhone:\n502-852-6495\nEmail:\ngraduate@louisville.edu\nHours:\nMonday \u2014 Friday\n9 a.m. to 4:30 p.m.\nNo holiday hours\nAddress:\nHouchens Bldg., Rm 105\n2211 S. Brook St.\nLouisville, KY 40292\nConnect with Graduate School\nfacebook\ninstagram\nyoutube\nlinkedin\nAdmissions\nAcademics & Research\nFunding, Tuition & Aid\nGraduate Student Life\nProfessional Development\nAbout Us\nSubmit a Story to the Graduate School News\nSubmit to our Newsletters\n\u00a9 2026 University of Louisville\nAccessibili